/-!
# Intrinsic three-prime local calculations in A7

This interface proves recognition of the three-generated subgroup from its
normal moving four-group and two-core index. The complete seven-point action
catalogue and concrete normalizer-residual calculations then identify an A4
residual's normalizer with the centralizer of an actual triple transposition,
equivalently the stabilizer of its partition of type 2,2,2,1. The action,
conjugation and residual identifications all retain the given permutation
embedding.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, 15.3.43, printed pp.1139–1140, with 1.1.5(3)(d),
printed pp.501–502 (combined manuscript, 1 March 2004).
-/
